  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRC Invest Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Democratic Republic of the Congo):  .USAID&apos;s DRC Invest activity aims to unlock $100 million in capital for Congolese agribusinesses and other enterprises. In addition to unlocking capital, DRC Invest attracts new impact investors to DRC, sustainably increasing Congolese businesses&apos; access to favorable financing to fuel business growth..With FY 2021 funds, DRC Invest identifies small and medium-sized businesses to increase their capacity and assist them with financing through an investment facilitation platform. In turn, these businesses benefit local communities and producers as they strengthen key sectors and value chains. DRC Invest helps deepen DRC&apos;s nascent financial markets and improves the business and investment ecosystem. The platform provides technical assistance to facilitate and expedite engagement between small businesses and risk-adverse finance providers. By utilizing market-led impact investment models, the activity strengthens the sustainability of investments in communities and regions that lack well-financed, resilient market systems..The activity contributes to the Mission&apos;s Integrated Country Strategy via Mission Goal 2 (Improved quality of life for Congolese through delivery of core services and expanded economic growth) and USAID&apos;s Country Development Cooperation Strategy via Development Objective 3 (Inclusive, broad-based, and sustainable economic growth increased). The activity fundamentally contributes to sustainable economic growth as facts that can further stimulate regional stability and enable economic growth, a critical U.S. foreign policy priority..</narrative>
  </description>
